1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,399
FloodGuard AI: an actual browser walkthrough. Models are assumed trained on small
datasets; all demonstrated readings are illustrative.

2
00:00:07,399 --> 00:00:15,724
National screening summarizes district risk, priorities, and monitoring intervals in
one command view.

3
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:26,823
The river summary compares city discharge and forecast values, with timestamps and a
manual refresh control.

4
00:00:26,823 --> 00:00:37,922
The rainfall table compares current, recent, and forecast rainfall across the four
operational cities.

5
00:00:37,922 --> 00:00:49,021
System information shows the configured data mode, monitoring interval, and active
risk engine.

6
00:00:49,021 --> 00:01:00,121
Toggle district boundaries, screening, waterways, catchments, and monitoring
categories on the interactive map.

7
00:01:00,121 --> 00:01:11,220
Compare the available Kashmir outlines and enable Flood Hub markers. The gauges shown
here are illustrative integration examples.

8
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:22,319
Enter latitude and longitude to inspect local coverage. The selected coordinate is
pinned on the map.

9
00:01:22,319 --> 00:01:33,418
Enable corresponding layers to focus on the selected district and hydrological sub-
basin, including matching river features.

10
00:01:33,418 --> 00:01:44,517
Hover and pin a priority monitoring station to inspect readings, provenance, and
stored trends.

11
00:01:44,517 --> 00:01:55,617
Station details link to an interactive forecast, separate historical series, date
inspection, a readings table, and CSV download.

12
00:01:55,617 --> 00:02:06,716
Inspect glacier coverage and upstream drainage, including glaciers that contribute to
Pakistan's river basins.

13
00:02:06,716 --> 00:02:17,815
Select a place to display a dated satellite water-mask overlay. This recording uses
an illustrative U-Net output.

14
00:02:17,815 --> 00:02:28,914
Switch between observed accumulation windows and 24-hour or 72-hour forecasts. Colors
follow the rainfall scale.

15
00:02:28,914 --> 00:02:40,013
GIS Operations estimates exposed people and mapped settlements, with district or
tehsil breakdowns and coverage information.

16
00:02:40,013 --> 00:02:51,113
The analysis supports historical water, configured segmentation, uploaded polygons,
and synthetic scenarios; inspect the existing result and its layers.

17
00:02:51,113 --> 00:03:02,212
Five predictive views cover riverine, flash, urban, seasonal basin, and upstream or
transboundary risk, with forecast times and target selectors.

18
00:03:02,212 --> 00:03:09,611
Riverine forecasts: XGBoost baseline inputs, Trimmu and Balloki targets, discharge
forecasts, and flood classes over 24–48 hours.

19
00:03:09,611 --> 00:03:17,011
Flash-flood guidance combines rainfall, soil moisture, and GIS features for catchment
risk within six hours.

20
00:03:17,011 --> 00:03:28,110
Urban susceptibility uses city-scale targets, rainfall, drainage context, and
selectable forecast intervals.

21
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:35,509
Seasonal basin risk shows forecasts over weeks to months, with target-specific risk
series.

22
00:03:35,509 --> 00:03:42,909
Upstream and transboundary risk highlights anomalous flow changes over hours to days.
Model outputs are illustrative in this demo.

23
00:03:42,909 --> 00:03:54,008
Select upper-basin stations, compare GloFAS and GEOGloWS series, and inspect
historical trends, rainfall, and forecast risk signals.

24
00:03:54,008 --> 00:04:01,408
Each station includes provider summaries, expected peaks, rainfall context, location
details, and scheduled or manual refresh.

25
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:12,507
Filter monitoring stations by river or name, switch units, and compare current flow,
forecasts, flood categories, and expected peaks.

26
00:04:12,507 --> 00:04:19,906
Open a station to inspect its upstream network and forecast. Chart legends and date
inspection help distinguish the displayed series.

27
00:04:19,906 --> 00:04:31,005
Citizen reports provide a scrollable database-backed feed, coordinates, optional
image or video links, priority flags, and closure status.

28
00:04:31,005 --> 00:04:42,105
Create a report using coordinates, browser location, or a Google Maps link. Image GPS
fields remain visible when no geotag is available.

29
00:04:42,105 --> 00:04:52,279
Flag a report for attention, then close it in the database. New reports appear in the
active window before remaining in the saved feed.

30
00:04:52,279 --> 00:05:03,378
Configure a station, measurement, units, test thresholds, and a reading profile to
exercise the monitoring workflow.

31
00:05:03,378 --> 00:05:10,777
Play the test scenario. Threshold crossings save simulated readings and create linked
alerts and incidents.

32
00:05:10,777 --> 00:05:18,177
Review threshold alerts, distinguish operational and simulated flows, and open the
linked incident.

33
00:05:18,177 --> 00:05:26,501
The incident view records severity, status, location, and timestamps. Linked details
preserve the simulated-flow context.

34
00:05:26,501 --> 00:05:33,901
The activity timeline records model decisions, monitoring changes, report actions,
and simulated response events.

35
00:05:33,901 --> 00:05:45,000
The walkthrough covers the portal as it runs in a web browser. Small-dataset training
is an assumption; this video does not validate model accuracy.
